%% DM26-0670

%% A client connects and registers, as built (2026-10-21, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md), with the identity
%% check on resuming a session that is designed (docs/architecture/policy-enforcement.md, stage 0) and not built yet.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (TcpClientActor)
    participant LM as ListenerManager
    participant Listener
    participant Broker
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgent

    Client->>LM: TCP connect, mutual TLS (the cluster's CA)
    LM->>LM: identity = the leaf's first DNS SAN (none: fails open, identity unset)<br/>designed: keep the leaf, for its p: names
    LM->>Listener: spawn, one per connection, with the identity
    Client->>Listener: RegistrationRequest(registration_id or none)
    Listener->>Broker: RegistrationRequest(client_id, registration_id, identity)
    Broker->>SM: handle_registration_request

    alt a registration_id that names a live or detached session
        rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
        Note over SM: DESIGNED: the connection's identity must be the session's,<br/>else this is a new session (a registration id is not a bearer token)
        end
        SM->>SA: resume, attach this connection
    else new
        SM->>SA: spawn SessionAgent(registration_id), Session { identity }
        SM->>SM: supersede older sessions of the same identity
    end
    SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(registration_id)
    Listener->>Listener: remember registration_id and the session's address
    Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok registration_id)
    Client->>Client: ClientEvent::Registered, the builder sends every subscription again
    Note right of Client: every subscribe and publish is then decided at the Listener<br/>(client_subscription, client_publish)
